  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "4.15.0: the Wasm backend now AUTO-VECTORIZES kernels to WebAssembly SIMD128 (v128) - a separate `kernel_simd` is generated alongside the scalar kernel and selected when the runtime supports SIMD (the scalar path stays byte-identical and first-class). Coverage is the complete per-lane kernel class: the full numeric tier (f32x4 / i32x4 / f64x2 / i64x2, the last two double-pumped) across elementwise code, counted loops, divergent if-diamonds, gather, scatter, conditional/masked stores, general acyclic divergent control flow (chained AND nested selects), and DIVERGENT LOOPS (a data-dependent branch inside a loop); plus the whole scalar-math surface (min/max/sqrt/floor/ceil, transcendentals sin/cos/exp/log/tanh, rcp/rsqrt, pow/atan2) on f32 and f64. Cross-mode deterministic (SIMD == scalar bit-exact). Group/barrier/atomic kernels keep their existing multi-worker path. Also: every in-register quant decoder (Float8E8M0 / Float4E2M1 / Float8E4M3 / Float8E5M2 RawBitsToFloat) is now single-exit/branchless, fixing a WebGL/GLSL shader-size explosion when a multi-exit decode is inlined before a loop (MXFP4/MXFP8 dequant). Full history: CHANGELOG.md at https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.ILGPU/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md",
